WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.757
Survey data is another common long form example.

00:00:03.757 --> 00:00:08.222
Suppose each row contains one respondent, one question, and one score.

00:00:08.222 --> 00:00:15.857
We may want one output row per respondent, with question one, question two, and question three as separate columns.

00:00:15.857 --> 00:00:23.497
If there is at most one score for each respondent and question combination, an aggregate such as maximum can place that

00:00:23.497 --> 00:00:28.062
single value into the correct column.

00:00:28.062 --> 00:00:29.552
The important assumption is uniqueness.

00:00:29.552 --> 00:00:38.092
If multiple answers exist for the same respondent and question, you need to decide how those multiple values should be

00:00:38.092 --> 00:00:39.610
handled.
